Notably, the new deal was brokered by TITLE 9 and Timless Music Group&#8217;s Stanley Brown, who wrote and produced on Sapp&#8217;s 1999 album Nothing Else Matters , which reached No. 6 on Top Gospel Albums.

&#8220;More than thirty years into my journey&nbsp;as an artist, every partnership I enter must be rooted in purpose, shared vision and mutual respect,&#8221; Sapp tells Billboard. &#8220;While Roc Nation Distribution is an undeniable force in the music industry, what truly stood out was the openness and collaborative spirit of their leadership team. I&#8217;m honored to partner with them and look forward to creating something impactful together as I step into this next chapter of my career.&#8221;

The set&#8217;s lead single, &#8220;He&#8217;s Not Finished,&#8221; will be available on Aug. 21, and fans can pre-save the single here . Sapp co-wrote the song with Stan Jones, who was recently honored at the 2026 BMI Trailblazers of Gospel Music Awards for his contributions to Mississippi Mass Choir&#8217;s Gospel Airplay-topping &#8220;Only One Way Home.&#8221;

Restoration does not currently have a set release date and is expected to arrive in fall 2026. Sapp crafted the record alongside longtime music director Curtis Lindsey and additional songwriters including Jones and Gus Lacy. Notably, the project serves as his first collection of new music following 2025&#8217;s If I Were An R&B Singer EP, which he released for Valentine&#8217;s Day as a &#8220;one-and-done project.&#8221;

&#8220;Marvin Sapp is a talented, award-winning artist whose impact spans generations,&#8221; Roc Nation Distribution president Krystian Santini says. &#8220;We are excited to work with Marvin and his team, welcome them to the Roc Nation Distribution family, and look forward to many more years and projects together.&#8221;

&#8220;He&#8217;s Not Finished&#8221; will be just the fourth gospel/inspirational single released via Roc Nation Distribution. With Restoration marking the platform&#8217;s first full-length gospel release, this new partnership with Sapp is the latest step in bolstering Roc Nation Distribution&#8217;s presence in the gospel scene.

“Timeless Music Group and TITLE 9 helped bring Roc Nation its first Grammy nomination in the gospel genre with the success of [2023&#8217;s Stanley Brown-led] &#8216;God Is Good,&#8217; opening the door to build something meaningful in this space,&#8221; says Brown, Timeless Music Group&#8217;s producer and CEO.

&#8220;That momentum led us to partner with legendary artists like Marvin Sapp, who are vital to the gospel music genre and to culture overall,&#8221; he continues. &#8220;Our vision is to establish Roc Nation’s presence in the gospel/Inspirational space with the highest level of credibility, excellence, and cultural impact. Together, TMG, TITLE 9, and Roc Nation are building what we believe is the future of the genre, and we are honored to have Marvin Sapp on this journey with us.&#8221;

Marvin Sapp has sent 14 records to the top 10 of Gospel Albums, including five chart-toppers, over the course of his three-decade career. In 2008, he earned the rare late &#8217;00s gospel crossover hit when his classic &#8220;Never Would Have Made It&#8221; reached No. 82. Both &#8220;Never Would&#8221; and &#8220;Praise Him In Advance&#8221; appear on Thirsty , which is Sapp&#8217;s longest-charting Billboard 200 album (86 weeks). Notably, he&#8217;s earned two top 10 entries on the all-genre album ranking: 2010&#8217;s Here I Am (No. 2) and 2012&#8217;s I Win (No. 9).
